  "caveats": [
    "Baseline hyper-parameters are library defaults and were not tuned. A tuned baseline could perform better, so this comparison should be read as 'the proposed model versus reasonable off-the-shelf baselines', not 'versus the best achievable baseline'.",
    "XGBoost is not installed in this environment; scikit-learn's GradientBoostingClassifier was substituted and is labelled as such.",
    "GradientBoostingClassifier and MLPClassifier have no class-weight parameter, so those two baselines run without the imbalance correction that every other model in the comparison receives.",
    "All baselines use the same subject-wise splits and the same training-split-fitted scaler as the deep variants."
